            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I do a lot of report style writing and need virtual indentation to provide readability in >1000 line files with headings. I need to keep indentation whitespaces out of the files however since it interferes with pretty export to other formats. (was able to switch to neovim since there's a good implementation of orgmode now :) )\n\nOut of necessity i hacked a personal addition to nvim orgmode virtual indent. My imlementation counts words and length of utf8 chars to place whitespace extmarks in the right positions to  create virtual indentation for long lines. This is quite resource heavy and slow (it is also difficult to test, buggy and becomes jittery if run with vim.schedule()).\n\n<img width=\"1313\" height=\"765\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8fa619c6-e412-47aa-86cf-21ce672582dd\" />\n\nMy usecases would be solved if breakindentopts had an option to respect whitespace in inline extmarks.\n\nAnother solution would be if there was an api-call to get information about where in the line linebreak has done the virtual break (this would makes it easier to place inline extmarks on the next virtual line). ",
